des an initial `topology` message to the cluster with\n39-a set of neighbors for each node to use. \n40-\n41-### RPC: Topology! \n42-\n43-A topology message is sent at the start of the test, after initialization,\n44-and informs the node of an optional network topology to use for broadcast.\n45-The topology consists of a map of node IDs to lists of neighbor node IDs. \n46-\n47-Request:\n48-\n49-```clj\n50-{:type (eq \"topology\"),\n51- :topology {java.lang.String [java.lang.String]},\n52- :msg_id Int}\n53-```\n54-\n55-Response:\n56-\n57-```clj\n58-{:type (eq \"topology_ok\"),\n59- #schema.core.OptionalKey{:k :msg_id} Int,\n60- :in_reply_to Int}\n61-```\n62-\n63-\n"}}
